  "sampling": [
    "--temp",
    "0.6",
    "--top-k",
    "20",
    "--top-p",
    "0.95",
    "--min-p",
    "0"
  ],
  "env": {
    "GGML_CUDA_BATCH_INVARIANT": "1",
    "LLAMA_RS_REPLAY": "1",
    "GGML_CUDA_SHARED_POOL": "1",
    "LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_UBATCH": "256",
    "LLAMA_ARG_CHECKPOINT_EVERY_NT": "8192",
    "GGML_CUDA_POOL_RESERVE_MIB": "96",
    "GGML_ESCHA_PREFILL": "i8",
    "GGML_ESCHA_I8_MIN_ROWS": "256"
  },
  "notes": "CaryPalmer / professorpalmer's Qwen3.8-27B at 2.47 bits per weight (L0xRE-V2 bit allocation, Escha W2 format, EXL3 trellis codec). Only its own engine loads it: kernel bin-kintsugi = their llama.cpp fork 5f393adb5 (release source, MIT), built for sm_86 (the A4500; their kernels target RTX 20/30/40, not the V100). Settings from their start-server.ps1 (engine switches as env); on 20 GB the whole K/V cache fits in VRAM, so their tiered RAM cache is not used. Chat template: the bundle's kintsugi.jinja. ts = A4500 only.",
  "configs": [
    {
